# E-commerce Funnel Analysis using SQL
This project analyses customer behaviour across an e-commerce conversion funnel using SQL.

PROJECT OVERVIEW
The objective is to identify user drop-off points, measure conversion rates, and evaluate performance across devices, channels, regions, and product categories.

## Dataset Source

Dataset sourced from Kaggle:

[E-commerce Funnel Analysis Dataset] https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/dhruvkp07/funnel-analysis-dataset
Dataset contains 21,409 customer interaction records across four funnel stages:

- Browse
- Add to Cart
- Checkout
- Purchase

Columns:
- User ID
- Session ID
- Event
- Device
- Region
- Channel
- Product Category
- Revenue
- Bonus Flag

BUSINESS QUESTIONS
1. What is the overall funnel conversion rate?
2. Which funnel stage has the highest drop-off?
3. Which device converts best?
4. Which marketing channel performs best?
5. Which region has the highest conversion rate?
6. Which product category converts best?

SQL TECHNIQUES USED
- CASE WHEN
- COUNT(DISTINCT)
- GROUP BY
- ORDER BY
- Aggregate Functions
- Data Quality Checks

KEY FINDINGS
- Overall Conversion Rate: 10.04%
- Highest Drop-off: Checkout → Purchase (70.95%)
- Best Device: Desktop (10.58%)
- Best Channel: Google Ads (10.63%)
- Best Region: South (10.54%)
- Best Product Category: Electronics (11.16%)

